Say whether the application asked to resize.

#255 comes down to one question that no amount of reading settles: MoneyMoney's Preferences window
never changes size when its pane changes, and the pane that visibly overflows is the one whose
overflow exceeds its own top padding. Either the application asks and the request dies somewhere,
or it never asks.

-[NSWindow setFrame:display:animate:] now prints the requested frame, whether it is a resize, and
whether there is a platform window to carry it, gated on CIDER_TRACE_TOOLBAR. That last field
matters: a request made before the window is mapped reaches nothing, and printing only the request
would make it look delivered.

It answers. Driving Preferences and clicking Security, every request for that window is:

    CIDER_SETFRAME class=MMWindow to={697.0,-24.0 406.0x346.0} didSize=1 platform=NIL
    CIDER_SETFRAME class=MMWindow to={697.0,-56.0 406.0x378.0} didSize=1 platform=NIL
    CIDER_SETFRAME class=MMWindow to={697.0,-9.0  406.0x331.0} didSize=1 platform=NIL

Three, all during setup, all before the platform window exists, ending at 331 which is the General
pane content of 253 plus 56 toolbar plus 22 title bar. AFTER THE CLICK THERE ARE NONE. The
application sizes this window once, to the first pane, and never again.

So the missing resize is not a request we drop. The surface faithfully carries the frame it is
given, which patch 0083 already established.

WHY THE PANES STILL MOSTLY LOOK RIGHT, measured from the nib by reading each pane by its CONTENTS
rather than by order, which is the mistake that made me withdraw this account once:

    obj[377] 406x253 six checkbox rows and a popup           GENERAL     overflow  0
    obj[352] 406x261 a scroll view and a help button         EXTENSIONS  overflow  8
    obj[423] 406x265 three checkboxes with captions          PAYMENTS    overflow 12
    obj[444] 406x286 one 371x40 label and a centred button   SECURITY    overflow 33

Every pane carries about 20 points of empty space above its topmost subview, so an overflow of 8 or
12 is absorbed and 33 is not. Four panes, four correct predictions, including the two that looked
like counterexamples when the sizes were assigned to the wrong panes.

Off by default.

Task #255.

--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -1256,6 +1256,18 @@
     [_backgroundView setFrameSize: _frame.size];
     [_platformWindow setFrame: _frame];
 
+    /* DOES THE APPLICATION ASK. MoneyMoney's Preferences never resizes when its pane changes, and
+     * the only pane that visibly overflows is the one whose overflow exceeds its own top padding
+     * (#255). This says whether the request arrives at all, and whether there was a platform
+     * window to carry it, because a request made before the window is mapped reaches nothing. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TOOLBAR") != NULL) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_SETFRAME class=%s to={%.1f,%.1f %.1fx%.1f} didSize=%d platform=%s\n",
+                object_getClassName(self), (double) newFrame.origin.x, (double) newFrame.origin.y,
+                (double) newFrame.size.width, (double) newFrame.size.height, (int) didSize,
+                _platformWindow != nil ? "yes" : "NIL");
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
     if (didSize) {
         [self resetCursorRects];
         [self postNotificationName: NSWindowDidResizeNotification];
